  "worked_solution": "Since $P(x)\u21d2Q(x)\u2261\u00acP(x)\u2228Q(x),$ the corresponding truth sets can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P\u21d2Q} & ={T}_{\u00acP\u2228Q} \\\\  & ={T}_{\u00acP}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & ={\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}={4,6,8,9,10}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, the complement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{P} & =\\overset{\u2015}{{4,6,8,9,10}} \\\\  & ={2,3,5,7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{Q}={2,5,10}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P\u21d2Q} & ={\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & ={2,3,5,7}\\cup {2,5,10} \\\\  & ={2,3,5,7,10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
